message:
A finished scan kept its read-ahead memory reservation with the
`TemporaryMemoryManager` until the query ended. With
`read_ahead_depth=-1` (the default), each read-ahead scan reserves at
least `min(8MB × threads, memory_limit / 16)` for its backlog, however
small its table is. Joins and aggregates that ran after it were granted
that much less memory and spilled when they did not need to.

`ScanReadAhead` now releases its memory governor once the scan is
exhausted, as `ManagedAsyncTaskQueue` and `ManagedAsyncWriteQueue`
already do when they finish. A scan that stops early (e.g. under a
`LIMIT`) still releases when it is destroyed, as before. For some
scenarios with tight memory, this PR can benefit them as an example
below.

### Reproducer

A fact table is joined to nine 100-row dimension tables, then grouped
into 30M groups. Each dimension scan holds its read-ahead reservation
until the query ends, so the aggregate gets about 576MB less memory and
spills.

Setup:

```sql
-- duckdb repro.db
CREATE TABLE fact AS SELECT range AS g, range % 100 AS k, range * 3 AS x FROM range(30000000);
CREATE TABLE d1 AS SELECT range AS k FROM range(100);
CREATE TABLE d2 AS FROM d1; CREATE TABLE d3 AS FROM d1; CREATE TABLE d4 AS FROM d1; CREATE TABLE d5 AS FROM d1;
CREATE TABLE d6 AS FROM d1; CREATE TABLE d7 AS FROM d1; CREATE TABLE d8 AS FROM d1; CREATE TABLE d9 AS FROM d1;
CHECKPOINT;
```

Query:

```sql
SET threads=8;
SET async_threads=4;
SET storage_block_prefetch='debug_force_always';
SET memory_limit='1700MB';
SET enable_profiling='json';
SET profiling_output='profile.json';
SET tracked_metrics=['system.total_bytes_spilled'];
.timer on
SELECT count(*), sum(s) FROM (
	SELECT g, sum(x) AS s
	FROM fact
	JOIN d1 USING (k) JOIN d2 USING (k) JOIN d3 USING (k) JOIN d4 USING (k) JOIN d5 USING (k)
	JOIN d6 USING (k) JOIN d7 USING (k) JOIN d8 USING (k) JOIN d9 USING (k)
	GROUP BY g
);
.timer off
SET enable_profiling='no_output';
SELECT system.total_bytes_spilled // 1000000 AS spilled_mb FROM read_json('profile.json');
```

Three runs each, on an 18-core Apple M5:
| | Time | Spilled |
|---|---|---|
| main | 0.28–0.32s | 346–379MB |
| this PR | 0.19–0.22s | 0MB |
